nk":26,"finishRateRank":78,"winningTimeRank":11,"winningTimeRankDir":4,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["up"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:27:42","holder":"Bruce FORDYCE","year":1988,"type":"up"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1952,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"07:00:02"}},"narrative":"The 1998 Comrades Marathon was the 73rd running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 87.300 km. The race was held on Tuesday, 16 June. Conditions: Clear, with warm sunshine. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nDmitri GRISHIN claimed the men's title in 05:26:25, ahead of Charl MATTHEUS (05:31:32) and Alexei Volgin (05:33:57). Rae BISSCHOFF won the women's race in 06:38:57, followed by Valentina LIAKHOVA (06:39:16).\n\nDmitri GRISHIN's 05:26:25 set a new up record, beating Bruce FORDYCE's 05:27:42 from 1988. Rae BISSCHOFF's 06:38:57 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nFrom a field of 13,368 entries, 10,490 runners crossed the finish line (78.5% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,207 men and 1,283 women (12.2% female). The average finish time was 09:40:43.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 645 Silver, 9,825 Bronze. 2,251 runners (21.5%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Michelle ROGERS in 10:59:59.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 37% of the finishers, with 6,570 seniors (avg 09:34:31) and 3,919 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}